"The `Group` class represents a group of users on the system. Contains common "
"properties for \n"
"        managing user permissions and relationships with the group. It "
"contains a `name` property to identify the group \n"
"        and also a  `permissions` field to define the permissions assigned "
"to the group. Users can be added to a group,\n"
"             which allows access to users belonging to a specific group. The "
"available groups are: `Financial Manager`,\n"
"              `Calculation Manager`, `Legal Manager`, `Financial "
"Consultant`, `Calculation Consultant` and \n"
"              `Legal Consultant`.\n"
"            "
